{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WoVQiTTsU4x647UrPq6Dt1","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→id: test-rel01.0\n     2→title: \"Test Suite: rel01.0 — wc specification and differential test\"\n     3→release: rel01.0\n     4→\n     5→traces:\n     6→  - rel01.0-uc001-wc\n     7→  - prd005-wc R1\n     8→  - prd005-wc R2\n     9→  - prd005-wc R3\n    10→  - prd005-wc R4\n    11→  - prd005-wc R5\n    12→  - prd005-wc R6\n    13→\n    14→preconditions:\n    15→  - ./bin/wc exists (built via mage build).\n    16→  - Reference binary gwc is installed via Homebrew (coreutils) and on PATH.\n    17→  - Tests are run via go test ./cmd/wc/... which invokes RunDiffTests from pkg/testutils.\n    18→  - All tests use LC_ALL=C to eliminate locale-dependent divergence.\n    19→  - \"wc: no normalization is applied; wc output is deterministic integer counts.\"\n    20→\n    21→test_cases:\n    22→  - name: wc_default_three_lines\n    23→    description: Default flags (line, word, byte count) with three-line stdin.\n    24→    inputs:\n    25→      args: []\n    26→      stdin: \"foo\\nbar baz\\nqux\\n\"\n    27→      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n    28→    normalization: none\n    29→    expected:\n    30→      exit_code: 0\n    31→      stdout_structure: 'output contains \"3\"'\n    32→      stderr: \"\"\n    33→    traces:\n    34→      - prd005-wc R1.1\n    35→      - prd005-wc R1.2\n    36→      - prd005-wc R1.3\n    37→\n    38→  - name: wc_lines_only\n    39→    description: -l flag counts newline characters only.\n    40→    inputs:\n    41→      args: [\"-l\"]\n    42→      stdin: \"one\\ntwo\\nthree\\n\"\n    43→      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n    44→    normalization: none\n    45→    expected:\n    46→      exit_code: 0\n    47→      stdout_structure: 'output contains \"3\"'\n    48→      stderr: \"\"\n    49→    traces:\n    50→      - prd005-wc R2.1\n    51→      - prd005-wc R2.6\n    52→\n    53→  - name: wc_words_only\n    54→    description: -w flag counts words (maximal sequences of non-whitespace).\n    55→    inputs:\n    56→      args: [\"-w\"]\n    57→      stdin: \"hello world\\ngoodbye  cruel   world\\n\"\n    58→      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n    59→    normalization: none\n    60→    expected:\n    61→      exit_code: 0\n    62→      stdout_structure: 'output contains \"5\"'\n    63→      stderr: \"\"\n    64→    traces:\n    65→      - prd005-wc R2.2\n    66→      - prd005-wc R2.6\n    67→\n    68→  - name: wc_bytes_only\n    69→    description: -c flag counts bytes.\n    70→    inputs:\n    71→      args: [\"-c\"]\n    72→      stdin: \"abc\\n\"\n    73→      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n    74→    normalization: none\n    75→    expected:\n    76→      exit_code: 0\n    77→      stdout_structure: 'output contains \"4\"'\n    78→      stderr: \"\"\n    79→    traces:\n    80→      - prd005-wc R2.3\n    81→\n    82→  - name: wc_chars_lc_c\n    83→    description: -m with LC_ALL=C; character count equals byte count under C locale.\n    84→    inputs:\n    85→      args: [\"-m\"]\n    86→      stdin: \"hello\\n\"\n    87→      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n    88→    normalization: none\n    89→    expected:\n    90→      exit_code: 0\n    91→      stdout_structure: 'output contains \"6\"'\n    92→      stderr: \"\"\n    93→    traces:\n    94→      - prd005-wc R2.4\n    95→      - prd005-wc R5.1\n    96→      - prd005-wc R5.2\n    97→\n    98→  - name: wc_max_line_length\n    99→    description: -L flag reports the longest line length with tab expansion.\n   100→    inputs:\n   101→      args: [\"-L\"]\n   102→      stdin: \"short\\na much longer line here\\nmed\\n\"\n   103→      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n   104→    normalization: none\n   105→    expected:\n   106→      exit_code: 0\n   107→      stdout_structure: 'output contains \"22\"'\n   108→      stderr: \"\"\n   109→    traces:\n   110→      - prd005-wc R2.5\n   111→\n   112→  - name: wc_combined_flags_order\n   113→    description: Combined flags (-l -w -c) produce counts in fixed order (lines, words, bytes).\n   114→    inputs:\n   115→      args: [\"-w\", \"-l\", \"-c\"]\n   116→      stdin: \"one two\\nthree\\n\"\n   117→      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n   118→    normalization: none\n   119→    expected:\n   120→      exit_code: 0\n   121→      stdout_structure: counts in order lines, words, bytes regardless of flag order\n   122→      stderr: \"\"\n   123→    traces:\n   124→      - prd005-wc R2.6\n   125→\n   126→  - name: wc_multi_file_total\n   127→    description: 'Two files produce per-file lines and a total line with right-aligned columns. Setup: file1.txt contains \"hello\\nworld\\n\" (2 lines, 2 words, 12 bytes), file2.txt contains \"foo bar baz\\n\" (1 line, 3 words, 12 bytes)'\n   128→    inputs:\n   129→      args: [\"file1.txt\", \"file2.txt\"]\n   130→      stdin: null\n   131→      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n   132→    normalization: none\n   133→    expected:\n   134→      exit_code: 0\n   135→      stdout_structure: three lines — file1 counts, file2 counts, total with label \"total\"; columns right-aligned\n   136→      stderr: \"\"\n   137→    traces:\n   138→      - prd005-wc R1.4\n   139→      - prd005-wc R3.1\n   140→      - prd005-wc R3.2\n   141→\n   142→  - name: wc_total_only\n   143→    description: '--total=only with two files prints only the total line. Setup: file1.txt contains \"a\\n\", file2.txt contains \"b\\nc\\n\"'\n   144→    inputs:\n   145→      args: [\"--total=only\", \"file1.txt\", \"file2.txt\"]\n   146→      stdin: null\n   147→      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n   148→    normalization: none\n   149→    expected:\n   150→      exit_code: 0\n   151→      stdout_structure: one line with summed counts and label \"total\"\n   152→      stderr: \"\"\n   153→    traces:\n   154→      - prd005-wc R3.3\n   155→\n   156→  - name: wc_total_never\n   157→    description: '--total=never with two files prints no total line. Setup: file1.txt contains \"x\\n\", file2.txt contains \"y\\n\"'\n   158→    in