{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01KrCrx86RQct44C9A9C5GVF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Implementation complete. `cmd/wc/main.go` implements all prd005-wc requirements:\n\n- **R1**: Default mode prints lines, words, bytes\n- **R2**: All flags (-l, -w, -c, -m, -L) with fixed output column order and -m/-c precedence\n- **R3**: Multi-file totals with `--total=auto|always|only|never` support, right-aligned columns\n- **R4**: Stdin (implicit and via `-`), binary input safety, empty input, `--files0-from`\n- **R5**: LC_ALL=C targeting where chars equal bytes\n- **R6**: Exit 0 on success, exit 1 on file errors or stdout write errors\n\nKey design choices:\n- GNU-compatible argument parsing with combined short flags (`-lwc`)\n- Field width computed from total file sizes (stat-based) with fallback to 7 for stdin/non-regular files\n- Byte-oriented counting matching GNU wc under LC_ALL=C (C-locale isspace semantics)\n- `pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` called at startup for silent broken-pipe exit"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":196,"cache_read_input_tokens":85341,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":196},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8a115c45-1bdc-4b94-a522-324914dd00d1","uuid":"7a90577b-c4e3-4676-9093-0fdfbdeec05b"}
